# Build output
**/.build/

# Per-machine VMB project configuration. VMBLauncher requires this exact file
# at ProjectRoot; copy .vmbrc.example to .vmbrc and customize the local copy.
.vmbrc

# VMB Launcher lives in its own repo at github.com/Ensrick/vmb-launcher.
# Kept here on disk for convenience; not tracked in this repo.
tools/vmb-launcher/

# Compiled Workshop bundles (generated by deploy scripts)
**/upload/content/

# Loose bundle files (hash-named build artifacts)
[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f]

# Pre-built distribution archives
*.zip
!qa/fixtures/recovery_manifests/producer-tracked.zip
!qa/fixtures/recovery_manifests/producer-receipt.zip

# Preprocessor output
*.lua.processed

# NOTE: CLAUDE.md and ANTIGRAVITY.md are intentionally TRACKED so AI-assistant
# context travels with the repo (maintainer request 2026-05-02). Machine setup
# belongs in ignored local configuration; see docs/PORTABLE_SETUP.md.

# Steam SDK artifact
upload/steam_appid.txt
.temp/

# Claude Code agent worktrees + local session state. Never tracked. Prior
# sessions left orphaned git worktrees here (15k+ stale .lua files) that
# inflated the static-scan file counts and timed out the pre-commit gate; the
# qa/check_*.ps1 scanners also skip this path via their exclusion chains (#727).
.claude/

# Documentation policy (PROJECT_STANDARDS.md §7.3 + §7.4):
# - Active investigation notes live in <mod>/_investigating/ and are ephemeral.
#   Findings get distilled into POSTMORTEMS.md (tracked) on resolution.
# - Audit snapshots (AUDIT_*.md) are point-in-time reports, not source of truth.
#   Findings get filed as GitHub Issues or distilled into postmortems/reference
#   docs; the snapshot itself is not committed.
**/_investigating/
**/AUDIT_*.md
**/_audit_*.md
**/_audit_*.py
**/_qa_*.md
**/_qa_*.py
**/_qa_*.json
OPEN_WORK_*.md

# Build/staging output
.release-stage/
__pycache__/

# Temp / backup files
**/*.lua.new
**/*.lua.bak*

# Local debug captures
**/_pc_b_logs/
**/pcb-log.log

# Local reference material (per-mod working copies of upstream sources)
**/.spawn_tweaks_ref/

# Multi-agent coordination sentinels (see CLAUDE.md § "Multi-agent coordination").
# The directory README is intentionally tracked so the convention is discoverable;
# individual sentinel files are ephemeral per-session claims and must not be committed.
.in_progress/*.md
!.in_progress/README.md

# Ship/version claim locks (see tools/ship/CLAIMS.md). The directory README is
# tracked so the on-disk format is discoverable; the .claim lock files are
# ephemeral per-session version-allocation state and must not be committed.
.ship_claims/*.claim
!.ship_claims/README.md

# REVIEW (2026-05-01):
# - bundleV2/ is INTENTIONALLY tracked (so other devs / git bisect can see the built bundle
#   that was deployed at each commit). Confirm with maintainer; if accidentally tracked, add
#   `**/bundleV2/` here.
# - .vmbrc is intentionally ignored. VMB has no base-plus-override merge; the
#   tracked .vmbrc.example is copied to the exact filename VMBLauncher expects.
# - bundleHistory.dat is tracked at repo root (binary, mtime old). Confirm intentional.
# - The 16-hex glob pattern correctly catches loose extensionless bundle artifacts but ALSO
#   catches any file with a 16-hex name in any directory (including bundleV2/ — but since
#   actual bundle files in bundleV2 have .mod_bundle extension, this is harmless).
# - dumps/ is tracked. Confirm intentional — these are large reference files generated from
#   in-game commands. Maybe `dumps/*.txt` should be ignored except a curated set?
# - launcher_screenshot.png (1MB) at repo root is tracked. Should it be moved to a docs/
#   subfolder?
# Sensitive paths check: no .env or credentials.json patterns ignored, but none exist in repo
# either. ugc_tool authenticates via Steam session, no token files written here.

# Retired-mod archives — kept on disk, never committed (repo convention:
# lobby_tweaker / la_prefix_patch / buff_tweaker all live here untracked)
_archive/

# Per-mod probe logs
**/.pcb_latest.log
